    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d25">

                <pb facs="0074" n="728" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg728"/>

                <head>No. 329.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hunter to Mr. Bassett.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-09-10"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 10,
                        1875</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 239.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With the instruction No. 237, of the 2d
                    instant, a copy of the note of Mr. Preston<anchor n="*" xml:id="d25-f1"/> to
                    this Department of the 26th ultimo, which concludes with a proposition in regard
                    to the refugees under your protection, was transmitted. A copy of the reply to
                    that note is inclosed.<anchor n="*" xml:id="d25-f2"/> It contains a counter
                    proposition upon the subject. The reply will without doubt be communicated by
                    Mr. Preston to his government. If the proposition should be acceptable to the
                    Haytian government, you are authorized and directed to see that it is complied
                    with according to its terms.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. HUNTER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
